# Talki repository rules

Before changing Talki application code, read:

- `/AGENTS.md`
- `/docs/design/landscape/README.md`
- `/docs/migration/landscape-roadmap.md`

The full canonical contract is in `AGENTS.md`.

Critical rules:

- Talki child UI is landscape-only on phones and tablets.
- Do not implement or preserve a portrait child layout.
- Current source code is the behavioral source of truth.
- `docs/design/landscape/reference/` is the visual source of truth.
- Preserve every existing game, category, practice mode, parent feature, reward feature, and behavior even if absent from a mock.
- Do not use the old `BottomNavigation` in the redesigned child experience.
- Responsive/device classification and orientation must be centralized.
- Never classify a landscape phone as a tablet by long-edge width alone.
- Do not scatter `Dimensions`, `useWindowDimensions`, arbitrary breakpoints, or local `isTablet` checks through feature screens.
- Do not duplicate whole phone/tablet screen trees.
- Hebrew RTL and logical start/end layout are required.
- Child controls require >= 48x48 dp effective touch targets.
- Never stretch artwork.
- Never use a reference screenshot itself as production UI.
- Preserve reducers/domain/audio/storage/progress logic unless the active phase explicitly changes behavior.
- Do not retire or delete the legacy Capacitor app during landscape phases.
- Never weaken tests just to make them pass.
- Implement one phase only, write its report, then stop.
